        "procedure": "To a methanol solution (15 mL) of 5-methylsalicylaldehyde (108 mg, 0.8 mmol) and Eu(CF3SO3)3 (60 mg, 0.1 mmol) was added dropwise 4,5-dimethyl-1,2-phenylenediamine (50 mg, 0.3 mmol) in methanol (10 mL) with stirring. The mixture was reacted for 3 days at room temperature and then kept at RT for slow evaporation. After 3 days, yellow single crystals suitable for X-ray diffraction were obtained.",
